1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,151
Marco 给团队发了这两段命令
Marco sent the team these two blocks of commands.

2
00:00:04,471 --> 00:00:08,532
它们会在他的笔记本电脑上启动 CareOneX 语音应用
They start the CareOneX voice app on his laptop.

3
00:00:08,852 --> 00:00:13,322
如果你看着像一堵乱码墙，这很正常
If they look like a wall of noise, that is normal.

4
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:18,428
看完这期视频，每一行你都会看懂
By the end of this video, every line will mean something.

5
00:00:18,748 --> 00:00:25,984
每一行背后，都是理解整个系统怎么拼在一起的一小课
Each one turns out to be a small lesson about how the whole system fits together.

6
00:00:26,233 --> 00:00:27,776
先提醒一句
One warning first.

7
00:00:27,826 --> 00:00:31,112
我们登录不了团队的 AWS 账号
We cannot log into the team's AWS account.

8
00:00:31,432 --> 00:00:37,486
所以这里的一切都来自 GitHub 上的代码和团队写的文档
So everything here is learned from the code on GitHub and the team's notes.

9
00:00:37,806 --> 00:00:39,926
每个说法都带一个标签
Each claim carries a tag,

10
00:00:39,926 --> 00:00:45,438
如果是我们推测的，标签会写 INFERRED（推测），并给出理由
and when we are guessing, the tag says INFERRED, with our reason.

11
00:00:46,483 --> 00:00:48,851
这两段命令启动两个程序
The two blocks start two programs.

12
00:00:49,171 --> 00:00:52,768
终端 1 启动 retrieve，一个小型检索服务器
Terminal 1 starts retrieve, a small search server.

13
00:00:53,088 --> 00:00:57,543
终端 2 启动 voice，也就是你真正对着说话的那个程序
Terminal 2 starts voice, the program you actually talk to.

14
00:00:57,783 --> 00:01:01,894
voice 听你的麦克风，再把回答播放出来
Voice listens to your microphone and plays the reply.

15
00:01:02,214 --> 00:01:06,817
需要查资料时，它就去问同一台电脑上的 retrieve
When it needs a fact, it asks retrieve, on the same laptop.

16
00:01:07,137 --> 00:01:11,033
两个程序还都会连到亚马逊的云，也就是 AWS
Both programs also talk to Amazon's cloud, AWS,

17
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:15,178
AI 模型和文档库都在那里
where the AI models and the document library live.

18
00:01:15,416 --> 00:01:17,204
终端（terminal）就是一个用打字
A terminal is a window

19
00:01:17,204 --> 00:01:20,779
输入命令、而不是用鼠标点的窗口
where you type commands instead of clicking.

20
00:01:21,099 --> 00:01:24,038
Marco 用的是 Windows 上的 PowerShell
Marco is on Windows, using PowerShell.

21
00:01:24,358 --> 00:01:28,286
从他命令的写法就能看出来
We can tell from the way his lines are written.

22
00:01:29,333 --> 00:01:32,422
第 1 行是 cd，意思是 change directory（切换目录）
Line 1 is cd, short for change directory.

23
00:01:32,742 --> 00:01:36,236
它把终端带进项目文件夹
It moves the terminal into the project folder.

24
00:01:36,556 --> 00:01:41,750
后面的每条命令，都以这个文件夹为起点去找文件
Every later command looks for its files relative to this folder.

25
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,423
这个文件夹是 Marco 自己的一份团队代码，里面有他最新的改动
The folder is Marco's own copy of the team's code, with his newest changes in it.

26
00:01:48,743 --> 00:01:50,143
这是我们推测的
We infer that,

27
00:01:50,143 --> 00:01:56,227
因为后面的命令需要的正好是团队仓库里的那些文件夹
because the next commands expect exactly the folders of the team repository.

28
00:01:57,267 --> 00:02:00,430
其余大部分行都长这样
Most of the other lines look like this:

29
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:04,405
美元符号、env、冒号、一个名字、等号、一个值
dollar sign, env, colon, a name, equals, a value.

30
00:02:04,725 --> 00:02:07,874
每一行设置一个环境变量（environment variable）
Each one sets an environment variable.

31
00:02:08,117 --> 00:02:13,190
可以把环境变量想成贴在终端窗口上的便利贴
Think of environment variables as sticky notes on the terminal window.

32
00:02:13,510 --> 00:02:17,292
从这个窗口启动的每个程序都能读到它们
Every program started from that window can read them.

33
00:02:17,612 --> 00:02:21,140
CareOneX 的代码就是这样读取设置的
The CareOneX code reads its settings this way,

34
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:25,512
所以代码里不会写死任何跟 Marco 电脑有关的东西
so nothing about Marco's laptop is written into the code.

35
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:28,861
便利贴只属于一个窗口
The notes belong to one window only.

36
00:02:29,181 --> 00:02:34,095
所以两段命令里都重复设置了同样的 AWS 那几行
That is why both blocks set the same AWS lines again.

37
00:02:35,133 --> 00:02:40,782
AWS 账号就是团队在亚马逊云里圈出来的一块自己的地方
An AWS account is the team's own fenced-off corner of Amazon's cloud.

38
00:02:41,102 --> 00:02:46,154
CareOneX 用到的所有东西都在里面，共用一张账单
Everything CareOneX uses lives inside it, and it has one bill.

39
00:02:46,474 --> 00:02:52,528
团队文档里写着：AI 模型的预算是每月 30 美元
The team's notes show a budget of 30 dollars a month for the AI models.

40
00:02:52,766 --> 00:02:54,405
没有人共用密码
Nobody shares a password.

41
00:02:54,725 --> 00:02:59,668
每个组员都通过一个统一登录门户，也就是 SSO（单点登录）
Each teammate signs in through a single sign-on portal, called SSO,

42
00:02:59,668 --> 00:03:02,692
用自己的邮箱加第二重验证登录
with their own email and a second factor.

43
00:03:03,012 --> 00:03:08,267
登录之后，每个人得到同一组权限，名字叫 AC215
After signing in, everyone gets the same set of permissions, named AC215.

44
00:03:08,587 --> 00:03:14,208
它包括 AI 模型、课程自己的存储和知识库
It covers the AI models, the course's own storage, and the knowledge base,

45
00:03:14,208 --> 00:03:17,853
但不包括公司生产环境里的任何东西
and nothing in the company's production systems.

46
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:22,642
profile（配置档）是电脑上一个设置文件里的一个有名字的条目
A profile is a named entry in a settings file on the laptop.

47
00:03:22,962 --> 00:03:24,602
“careonex-team”的意思是
"careonex-team" says:

48
00:03:24,602 --> 00:03:30,693
通过那个门户，登录团队账号，使用 AC215 权限
log in through that portal, into the team account, with the AC215 permissions.

49
00:03:31,013 --> 00:03:35,436
aws sso login 这条命令会打开浏览器，你点同意
The command aws sso login opens a browser, you approve,

50
00:03:35,436 --> 00:03:40,019
电脑就拿到一把有效期 8 小时的临时钥匙
and the laptop receives temporary keys that last 8 hours.

51
00:03:40,266 --> 00:03:45,484
CareOneX 的代码通过 profile 的名字找到这些临时钥匙
The CareOneX code finds those temporary keys through the profile name.

52
00:03:45,804 --> 00:03:53,136
钥匙过期后，voice 程序会停下来，用一行提示告诉你重新登录
When they expire, the voice program stops with a one-line message telling you to log in again.

53
00:03:54,183 --> 00:03:58,652
AWS 在世界各地的很多区域（region）都有数据中心
AWS runs data centers in many regions around the world.

54
00:03:58,972 --> 00:04:02,243
每个区域都是一套独立的云
Each region is its own copy of the cloud.

55
00:04:02,563 --> 00:04:08,860
团队的模型和存储都在 us-east-1，也就是北弗吉尼亚
The team's models and storage are all in us-east-1, in Northern Virginia,

56
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:12,483
所以每个程序都得被告知去那里
so every program must be told to go there.

57
00:04:13,517 --> 00:04:16,892
接下来是最奇怪的一行：把 HOME 设成 HOME
Now the strangest line: set HOME to HOME.

58
00:04:17,212 --> 00:04:19,619
看起来什么也没做
It looks like it does nothing.

59
00:04:19,939 --> 00:04:22,314
其实它修的是一个 Windows 上的问题
It fixes a Windows problem.

60
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:26,058
retrieve 程序会在一个容器（container）里运行
The retrieve program will run inside a container,

61
00:04:26,058 --> 00:04:27,658
就像一个密封的盒子
a sealed box.

62
00:04:27,757 --> 00:04:31,586
要用你的登录，盒子需要拿到你放钥匙的文件夹
To use your login, the box needs your keys folder.

63
00:04:31,906 --> 00:04:34,216
团队的 Docker 配置文件是通过
The team's Docker file finds

64
00:04:34,216 --> 00:04:37,682
一个叫 HOME 的变量找到这个文件夹的
that folder through a variable named HOME.

65
00:04:37,917 --> 00:04:40,346
在 Mac 上，HOME 一直都有
On a Mac, HOME is always set.

66
00:04:40,666 --> 00:04:42,558
在 Windows 上却没有
On Windows it is not,

67
00:04:42,558 --> 00:04:48,594
于是盒子会去一个空路径里找钥匙，登录就失败了
so the box would look for keys in an empty path and fail to log in.

68
00:04:48,914 --> 00:04:52,860
这一行把 PowerShell 自己知道的用户文件夹
The line copies PowerShell's own home folder

69
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:55,192
抄到 HOME 这张便利贴上
into the HOME sticky note.

70
00:04:55,512 --> 00:05:01,194
只有终端 1 需要它，因为只有终端 1 用了 Docker
Only terminal 1 needs it, because only terminal 1 uses Docker.

71
00:05:02,233 --> 00:05:05,134
Knowledge Base（知识库）是亚马逊的一项服务
A Knowledge Base is an Amazon service

72
00:05:05,134 --> 00:05:12,346
它把团队的文档存成一小段一小段可检索的文字，有人问就去搜
that stores the team's documents as small searchable passages, and searches them on request.

73
00:05:12,666 --> 00:05:17,365
每个知识库都有一个 ID，就是像这样的一串短代码
Every knowledge base has an ID, a short code like this one.

74
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:21,776
retrieve 的代码会先找这张便利贴
The retrieve code looks for this sticky note first.

75
00:05:22,096 --> 00:05:28,025
如果没有，它就去团队存储里的一个文件读 ID
If it is missing, it reads the ID from a file in the team's storage,

76
00:05:28,025 --> 00:05:32,732
这个文件是搭建资料库的那个容器写进去的
written there by the container that built the library.

77
00:05:32,966 --> 00:05:34,554
为什么要手动设置？
Why set it by hand?

78
00:05:34,604 --> 00:05:36,777
我们之前猜了两个原因
We had guessed two reasons:

79
00:05:36,777 --> 00:05:43,376
省掉一次读存储，或者让 retrieve 指向另一个知识库
to save one read from storage, or to point retrieve at a different knowledge base.

80
00:05:43,696 --> 00:05:47,553
Marco 当天晚些时候推送的分支给出了答案
Marco's branch, pushed later that day, settles it.

81
00:05:47,873 --> 00:05:51,640
这个 ID 是他为了比较几种切分
This ID is one of three test libraries he built

82
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:54,925
文档的方法而建的三个测试资料库之一
to compare ways of cutting the documents.

83
00:05:55,245 --> 00:05:59,512
没有这一行，retrieve 就会用主资料库
Without this line, retrieve would use the main library.

84
00:05:59,832 --> 00:06:02,126
第 6 集会讲他的这个测试
Episode 6 explains his test.

85
00:06:03,167 --> 00:06:08,466
Docker 把一个程序和它需要的一切打包成一个镜像（image）
Docker packs a program with everything it needs into an image,

86
00:06:08,466 --> 00:06:10,517
就像一个冷冻好的便当盒
like a frozen lunch box.

87
00:06:10,837 --> 00:06:13,480
容器就是这个盒子跑起来的样子
A container is that box, running.

88
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:19,204
它在 Marco 的电脑上、你的电脑上、服务器上，运行起来都一样
It runs the same on Marco's laptop, on yours, and on a server.

89
00:06:19,450 --> 00:06:24,652
docker compose 读取团队那个描述所有容器的文件
Docker compose reads the team's file that describes all the containers.

90
00:06:24,972 --> 00:06:26,572
up 表示启动
The word up starts one.

91
00:06:26,813 --> 00:06:29,940
build 这个选项会先重新构建镜像
The option build first rebuilds its image,

92
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:32,398
这样 Marco 最新的代码就在里面
so Marco's newest code is inside.

93
00:06:32,718 --> 00:06:35,940
而 retrieve 表示只启动检索服务器这一个
And retrieve picks just the search server.

94
00:06:36,184 --> 00:06:40,338
在盒子里，retrieve 变成一个小小的网页服务器
Inside the box, retrieve becomes a small web server.

95
00:06:40,658 --> 00:06:43,883
它在 8080 端口（port）上等待，端口就像一扇编了号的门
It listens on port 8080, a numbered door.

96
00:06:44,203 --> 00:06:49,832
Docker 配置文件把这扇门接到电脑上同一个号码的门
The Docker file connects that door to the same door on the laptop,

97
00:06:49,832 --> 00:06:52,221
这样别的程序就能来敲门
so other programs can knock.

98
00:06:53,267 --> 00:06:57,950
在终端 2，第一张新便利贴告诉 voice：retrieve 在哪儿
In terminal 2, the first new note tells voice where retrieve is.

99
00:06:58,270 --> 00:07:01,414
127.0.0.1 永远指的是这台电脑本身
127.0.0.1 always means this same computer,

100
00:07:01,414 --> 00:07:04,184
8080 就是 retrieve 打开的那扇门
and 8080 is the door retrieve opened.

101
00:07:04,504 --> 00:07:10,662
没有这张便利贴，语音应用就会回答说知识库不可用
Without this note, the voice app answers that the knowledge base is unavailable.

102
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:13,860
下一张便利贴决定语音应用怎么检索
The next note picks how voice searches.

103
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:18,781
我们第一次查的时候，GitHub 的代码里根本找不到它
When we first looked, it was nowhere in the code on GitHub.

104
00:07:19,101 --> 00:07:23,046
Marco 当天晚些时候推送的分支解释了它
Marco's branch, pushed later that day, explains it.

105
00:07:23,366 --> 00:07:28,951
feedback 先检索一次，可能再加一次，然后合并结果
Feedback runs a first search, may add one more, and merges the results.

106
00:07:29,271 --> 00:07:31,493
baseline 只检索一次
Baseline runs one search only.

107
00:07:31,813 --> 00:07:36,003
没有这张便利贴时，默认也是 feedback
Feedback is also the default when the note is missing.

108
00:07:36,323 --> 00:07:38,702
第 6 集会讲它具体做了什么
Episode 6 shows what it does.

109
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:42,265
最后一行最长
The last line is the longest.

110
00:07:42,585 --> 00:07:45,662
我们把它拆开来看。uv 是一个工具
Let's take it apart. uv is a tool

111
00:07:45,662 --> 00:07:50,385
它把项目需要的那个 Python 版本和那些库准备好
that sets up the exact Python and libraries a project needs,

112
00:07:50,385 --> 00:07:53,376
再在这个环境里运行命令
then runs a command inside that setup.

113
00:07:53,696 --> 00:07:58,938
Python 3.12 是亚马逊那个流式传输库能接受的最低版本
Python 3.12 is the oldest version Amazon's streaming library accepts.

114
00:07:59,258 --> 00:08:03,469
directory 选项的意思是：用 voice 这个项目
And the directory option says: use the voice project.

115
00:08:03,717 --> 00:08:06,421
extra mic 会额外装上麦克风库
extra mic adds the microphone library.

116
00:08:06,741 --> 00:08:12,132
它故意做成可选的：容器里没有麦克风也没有扬声器
It is optional on purpose: a container has no microphone or speakers,

117
00:08:12,132 --> 00:08:16,586
所以 voice 程序直接在电脑上跑
so the voice program runs directly on the laptop instead.

118
00:08:16,833 --> 00:08:20,721
最后，引号里的部分是一个很小的 Python 程序
Finally, the quoted part is a tiny Python program

119
00:08:20,721 --> 00:08:23,101
作用是启动语音会话
that starts the voice session.

120
00:08:23,421 --> 00:08:27,136
团队的说明文档用的是一条更短的命令
The team's instructions use a shorter command,

121
00:08:27,136 --> 00:08:31,498
但它会先检查一种保存下来的钥匙文件
but that one first checks for a kind of saved key file

122
00:08:31,498 --> 00:08:34,325
而 SSO 登录可能根本不会生成这种文件
that an SSO login may never create.

123
00:08:34,645 --> 00:08:38,148
直接调用会话，就跳过了这个检查
Calling the session directly skips that check.

124
00:08:38,468 --> 00:08:42,373
这是我们的推测，但和代码完全吻合
That is our inference; it fits the code exactly.

125
00:08:43,417 --> 00:08:45,806
放在一起，就是这样
Put together, it looks like this.

126
00:08:46,126 --> 00:08:48,754
两个程序都用你那 8 小时的登录
Both programs use your 8-hour login.

127
00:08:49,074 --> 00:08:52,626
你说话，voice 把声音实时传给 Nova 2 Sonic
You speak, voice streams it to Nova 2 Sonic,

128
00:08:52,626 --> 00:08:56,016
Nova 要查资料，voice 就去问 retrieve
Nova asks for a fact, voice asks retrieve,

129
00:08:56,016 --> 00:09:01,264
retrieve 去搜知识库，然后 Nova 把答案说出来
retrieve searches the knowledge base, and Nova speaks the answer.

130
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:06,499
这期视频里所有的新词，都在这一张卡片上
Here is every new word from this video on one card.

131
00:09:06,819 --> 00:09:10,298
想留着的话，可以在这里暂停
Pause here if you want to keep it.

132
00:09:10,534 --> 00:09:17,973
下一集讲全局：CareOneX 是干什么的，团队里谁做了哪一部分
Next, the big picture: what CareOneX is for, and who on the team built which part.
